00:00:42.480 --> 00:00:45.790
Number 5 - The Iron Bank Will Have It’s
Due

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:49.739
It was so awesome to finally get to visit
Braavos, we didn’t see a lot of the city

00:00:49.739 --> 00:00:53.719
outside of the Iron Bank, but I talked about
some of the other locations in my bonus video.

00:00:53.719 --> 00:00:55.469
I’ll have a link to that at the end.

00:00:55.469 --> 00:01:00.340
But the really important take aways from the
Bank Scene are that The Iron Bank is funding

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:04.750
Stannis, not because it cares about Tommen
being a bastard but because the Bank only

00:01:04.750 --> 00:01:06.110
trusts Tywin Lannister.

00:01:06.110 --> 00:01:11.960
But because he’s in his late 60s he’ll
be gone before the Crown’s debt is paid

00:01:11.960 --> 00:01:12.960
back.

00:01:12.960 --> 00:01:15.520
And everyone else in King’s Landing is terrible
at managing a kingdom.

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:19.390
So Stannis is the only viable contender for
the throne that actually has the skills to

00:01:19.390 --> 00:01:23.380
rule AND, very big AND pay back the debt.

00:01:23.380 --> 00:01:26.320
So they give him money to raise another army.

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:30.470
There were so many awesome callbacks to big
events in previous seasons, my favorite was

00:01:30.470 --> 00:01:33.220
Mark Gatiss, who’s playing Tycho Nestoris,
calls Davos out for all the ships resting

00:01:33.220 --> 00:01:34.710
at the bottom of Blackwater Bay.

00:01:34.710 --> 00:01:35.710
Ouch.

00:01:35.710 --> 00:01:37.840
One of his sons is down there too ya know.

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:40.979
It was really Davos that did the heavy lifting
in that meeting.

00:01:40.979 --> 00:01:45.009
Him showing his missing finger joints was
evidence of Stannis’ commitment to honoring

00:01:45.009 --> 00:01:46.009
debts.

00:01:46.009 --> 00:01:49.650
I’ll bet if he doesn’t repay the crown’s
debt and what he just borrowed.

00:01:49.650 --> 00:01:54.409
The Iron Bank will take his finger joints
just like Stannis took Davos’.

00:01:54.409 --> 00:01:59.640
Shout out for Salladhor Saan who’s not our
friend anymore, my friend.

00:01:59.640 --> 00:02:02.450
Number 4 - Drogon Destroys the Herd Of Sheep

00:02:02.450 --> 00:02:05.780
Really awesome scene from the book but there
was a really big change.

00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:08.850
In the book, those bones were of his child.

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:12.700
The picture on my television set was kind
of fuzzy, but I thought I did see a little

00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:15.250
boy’s ribcage, but I didn’t see a skull.

00:02:15.250 --> 00:02:19.770
And when she offers to pay him for his trouble
there’s nothing on her face that looks like

00:02:19.770 --> 00:02:23.640
the regret you have when your baby kills another
baby.

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:27.599
Plus during the actual scene, all we saw was
Drogon crest the hill and burn the goats.

00:02:27.599 --> 00:02:29.360
We never saw the boy catch fire.

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:32.310
Even though I don’t think they’re allowed
to do that on television.

00:02:32.310 --> 00:02:33.970
Even if they wanted to.

00:02:33.970 --> 00:02:38.200
It was a very brief, but very big moment for
establishing that Daenerys’ dragons do as

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:39.200
they please now.

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:40.490
And they’re starting to menace the country.

00:02:40.490 --> 00:02:42.980
It’s only going to get worse from here.

00:02:42.980 --> 00:02:47.780
Following that up was the first appearance
of Hizdhar zo Loraq who had a very big speaking

00:02:47.780 --> 00:02:50.430
role, I think it’s a good sign that he’ll
be back soon.

00:02:50.430 --> 00:02:54.099
If you’re not familiar with his character,
he’s the son of one of the former slave

00:02:54.099 --> 00:02:55.099
masters.

00:02:55.099 --> 00:02:56.470
Those are the wealthy families of the city.

00:02:56.470 --> 00:02:58.450
So he has a lot of influence in Meereen.

00:02:58.450 --> 00:03:00.830
I’ll talk about him more then next time
he’s in an episode.

00:03:00.830 --> 00:03:04.180
If you have read the books, let me know if
you think they should have added a couple

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:08.140
lines about the bones being the goat herder’s
son.

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:10.030
Number 3 - My Name Is Reek

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:13.450
I’ve been waiting so long for him to start
saying that.

00:03:13.450 --> 00:03:17.750
Essentially the whole Yara Ironborn invasion
was meant to show us how complete Reek’s

00:03:17.750 --> 00:03:19.290
transformation had become.

00:03:19.290 --> 00:03:21.510
The Theon that we knew is completely gone.

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:23.610
He’s even forgotten what a Bath is.

00:03:23.610 --> 00:03:27.790
And he lives with the dogs and enjoys it.

00:03:27.790 --> 00:03:29.879
I really liked how uncomfortable that bath
scene was.

00:03:29.879 --> 00:03:33.980
We’re supposed to feel horrified.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:38.140
The real twist is that Ramsay is going to
use Theon to take back Winterfell.

00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:41.230
By playacting as Theon Greyjoy.

00:03:41.230 --> 00:03:44.239
Only someone as mad as Ramsay could come up
with a plan like that.

00:03:44.239 --> 00:03:45.849
My name is Reek it rhymes with Freak.

00:03:45.849 --> 00:03:50.709
Feel free to write your favorite Reek rhymes
in the comments.

00:03:50.709 --> 00:03:52.489
Number 2 - Tyrion’s Trial Begins

00:03:52.489 --> 00:03:53.730
Because the Trial was so important and so
much was going on I separated it into two

00:03:53.730 --> 00:03:54.730
big moments.

00:03:54.730 --> 00:03:55.730
My number two is essentially the first montage.

00:03:55.730 --> 00:04:00.470
It’s like Cersei found every person at court
that Tyrion ever looked sideways at.

00:04:00.470 --> 00:04:05.319
Ser Meryn Trant was getting revenge for Tyrion
threatening him back in Season 2 when Joffrey

00:04:05.319 --> 00:04:07.560
was going to shoot Sansa with his crossbow.

00:04:07.560 --> 00:04:12.220
Maester Pycelle claims Tyrion stole The Strangler
poison from his stores when he threw him in

00:04:12.220 --> 00:04:14.290
the Black Cells, also back in season 2.

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:26.160
Then Cersei spits his Blackwater Joy to Ashes
speech back in his face and Varys talks about

00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:31.250
that small council meeting right after the
Red Wedding.

00:04:31.250 --> 00:04:34.639
No one is speaking falsely, with the exception
of Pycelle, he never stole poison.

00:04:34.639 --> 00:04:40.199
But Tyrion really did say all those things.

00:04:40.199 --> 00:04:47.240
and my Number 1 WTF moment - Tyrion Confesses

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:51.710
Tyrion’s outburst really was the best performance
in the episode.

00:04:51.710 --> 00:04:56.360
If there’s an acting contest going on between
the cast members, Peter Dinklage just won

00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:57.360
it.

00:04:57.360 --> 00:05:00.590
And just to be clear, he wasn’t confessing
to killing Joffrey.

00:05:00.590 --> 00:05:04.800
That was another change from the books.

00:05:04.800 --> 00:05:08.440
On the show, he just causes a huge scene and
demands trial by combat.

00:05:08.440 --> 00:05:15.870
Remember, that’s how he met Bronn in the
Eyrie in season 1.

00:05:15.870 --> 00:05:22.820
But that throws Jaime’s bargain with Tywin
out the window.

00:05:22.820 --> 00:05:29.389
The interesting thing here is that one, Shae
is clearly being manipulated by Cersei to

00:05:29.389 --> 00:05:30.389
lie.

00:05:30.389 --> 00:05:32.880
Did you see how many times she glanced at
her during her speech?

00:05:32.880 --> 00:05:38.100
And two, Tywin is so rigid in sticking to
the rules that he can’t save Tyrion.

00:05:38.100 --> 00:05:40.740
He has to allow the Trial by combat to commence.

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:42.930
He really was going to uphold his bargain
with Jaime.

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:44.120
And that’s why I love Game of Thrones so
much.

00:05:44.120 --> 00:05:47.030
It’s like one character or a group of characters
comes up with a really good plan to save the

00:05:47.030 --> 00:05:48.030
day.

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:51.550
And one person just says Fuck It, and things
just go to shit.

00:05:51.550 --> 00:05:53.900
It’s how Ned Stark ended up losing his head.

00:05:53.900 --> 00:05:57.310
Remember, in that instance Joffrey was the
one that went rogue.

00:05:57.310 --> 00:06:00.990
It was how Theon got into trouble when he
left to sack Winterfell.

00:06:00.990 --> 00:06:03.870
He could have just stayed and been a prince
for the rest of his life.

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:04.870
But nope.

00:06:04.870 --> 00:06:07.150
So let this be a lesson, if you’re a character
on Game of Thrones.

00:06:07.150 --> 00:06:09.100
And you’re part of some elaborate plan.

00:06:09.100 --> 00:06:10.100
Do not go rogue.

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:11.150
Stick to the plan.

00:06:11.150 --> 00:06:15.160
So let me know what you’re biggest WTF moment
was.

00:06:15.160 --> 00:06:16.540
Tyrion’s confession?

00:06:16.540 --> 00:06:18.600
Stannis in Braavos?

00:06:18.600 --> 00:06:20.710
Or just seeing what’s happening to Reek.

00:06:20.710 --> 00:06:23.060
It really is depressing to watch his scenes
this season.

00:06:23.060 --> 00:06:24.639
Just so horrible.

00:06:24.639 --> 00:06:28.880
The only real plot line that we need to remember
that I didn’t already mention is Oberyn

00:06:28.880 --> 00:06:30.660
Martell’s secret mission to kill the Mountain.

00:06:30.660 --> 00:06:34.810
There was a nice shoutout for Team Fuck The
King in that small council meeting too.

00:06:34.810 --> 00:06:38.680
I just love that Varys actually said it out
loud.

00:06:38.680 --> 00:06:40.759
There is now a bounty on The Hound.

00:06:40.759 --> 00:06:42.729
So more people will be trying to kill him.

00:06:42.729 --> 00:06:44.940
They don’t know Arya is with him.

00:06:44.940 --> 00:06:49.930
Oberyn was one of the few people at Tyrion’s
trial that was impartial, and his ears really

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:52.250
perked up when he heard Trial by Combat.

00:06:52.250 --> 00:06:54.509
We have seen scenes of him fighting in the
trailer.

00:06:54.509 --> 00:06:57.720
So that sounds like it’s right around the
corner.

00:06:57.720 --> 00:07:02.590
If there’s any big plot threads I missed
just add them in the comments.

00:07:02.590 --> 00:07:08.710
Overall the episode was another solid A. All
of the actors were amazing and Mark Gatiss

00:07:08.710 --> 00:07:12.169
was so much fun as Mycroft in Braavos.

00:07:12.169 --> 00:07:13.940
I really hope he comes back soon.

00:07:13.940 --> 00:07:16.770
Peter Dinklage was really the home run of
the episode.

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:21.400
He did an interview where he and Nikolaj Coster-Waldau
talked about joking around while they were

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:23.530
filming that trial scene.

00:07:23.530 --> 00:07:28.349
Because it was so emotionally demanding on
them, they tried to blow off steam by burning

00:07:28.349 --> 00:07:33.139
a few takes skipping down the aisle and laughing.

00:07:33.139 --> 00:07:37.319
But the funny part was that the whole crew
just looked daggers at them and no one on

00:07:37.319 --> 00:07:38.340
set laughed.

00:07:38.340 --> 00:07:42.449
They work like 18 hours a day when they shoot,
so who can blame them for getting upset when

00:07:42.449 --> 00:07:43.449
actors waste time?

00:07:43.449 --> 00:07:46.949
I’ve been so impressed this season with
how the producers have been able to include

00:07:46.949 --> 00:07:50.280
all these Holy Shit moments without things
getting out of control.

00:07:50.280 --> 00:07:55.569
It’s like we’re getting four or five Blackwater
level episodes instead of just one or two.

00:07:55.569 --> 00:07:58.610
Also, they’ve even started scouting locations
for season 5.

00:07:58.610 --> 00:08:00.710
I’ll talk about that in another video.

00:08:00.710 --> 00:08:06.550
In the teaser for episode 7 we saw the new
mountain, so we’ll get to see Tyrion’s

00:08:06.550 --> 00:08:11.039
trial by combat and it looks like Sansa gets
another peek at the Moon Door.

